==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|kibbitzer}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|kibitz|er|id2=agent noun}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who offers unsolicited views, advice, or criticism; one who [[kibitz]]es.
#: {{ux|en|Did I ask you what you thought about my cards, you '''kibitzer'''?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Anatole Broyard|title=Updike Goes All Out at Last|section=Books of The Times|work=The New York Times|date=1971-11-05|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1971/11/05/archives/updike-goes-all-out-at-last.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Neither good nor evil exactly, he is the ultimate catalyst or '''kibitzer''', a blue-note howl of pain and laughter such as Charlie Parker might have blown.}}

